# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14, F30); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: Safari is docked between Notes and the Desktop, where a calculator floats. A video goes full
# screen with the green button. Arbor leaves it to macOS: it keeps its place, is not turned into a tile,
# and commands on it are refused. When it comes back, everything is where it was.
# Reference: T63.
open Notes
open Safari
open Calculator 300x400
dock 101 left
dock 102 beside 101 right
expect left-of 101 102
expect floating 103
fullscreen 102 on
# Still docked, taking no space, and not Arbor's to move.
expect docked 102
expect hidden 102
expect count docked 2
zoom 102
expect fail
float 102
expect fail
resize 102 right 50
expect fail
dock 102 left
expect fail
expect docked 102
fullscreen 102 off
# Known (board 1.21): it is laid out as if alone before its neighbours are reported back, and then again.
expect jolt 102
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect left-of 101 102
expect floating 103
# Not taken for a window that refuses to shrink: it can be framed and goes back.
zoom 102
expect fills 102
back
expect left-of 101 102
# A floating window does the same, and returns to where its owner left it.
move 103 1000 300 300 400
fullscreen 103 on
expect floating 103
expect hidden 103
fullscreen 103 off
expect visible 103
expect left-of 102 103
# Misspelt, it says how.
fullscreen 103 maybe
expect fail
fullscreen 999 on
expect fail
